--- Surface (production-polished native parity, no stubs) ---------------------------------------------
WinUI 3 ContentControl over the shared InboxBodyViewModel (P1/S8 state-holder seam); no HTTP in the view.
Composes the glass inbox panel InboxBody owns: header (select-all checkbox [flat], live "{n} notifications"
count, grouped/flat view toggle [inbox tab], mark-all-read), a bulk-selection toolbar (mark read + archive on
the inbox, restore on the archive, delete on both, with a delete confirmation), and a body that renders every
state from the web source:
  loading  -> skeleton rows (live region)
  error    -> TsQueryError with Retry (cache-then-network hard failure)
  empty    -> friendly TsEmptyState: inbox / archived / grouped copy variants, CTA event seam
  loaded   -> day-grouped flat list (Today / Yesterday / dated headers, web groupByDay) OR threaded grouped list
  stale    -> content + freshness chip   |   offline -> content + offline chip (native cache-then-network)
Each row: severity chip (critical->danger, warn->warning, info->info, none->neutral), unread dot + bold title,
relative time, selection checkbox, and a context menu (mark read/unread, archive/restore, view context when the
row has an alert, delete). Auto-mark-read-on-open is reproduced for the flat inbox (opt-out via AutoMarkOnOpen).
Data binds the web hooks to the shared layer: useNotificationLogs/useNotificationGroups -> InboxSource (one
GET /notifications/logs read, ?grouped=true for threads); useMark*/useBulkMarkRead/useArchive/useUnarchive/
useDelete -> InboxCommands (post_api_v1_notifications_{mark_read,mark_unread,archive,unarchive}, delete logs).
i18n: every string from the source resolves through ILocalizer (PassthroughLocalizer in tests; resw in app);
no English literals in native code. a11y: Narrator names on the surface, every row, every interactive element;
reduce-motion honoured via TsFadeIn/TsSkeleton. Diagnostics: emits only "view.opened slug=InboxBody" (PII-safe).

